{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/291929-aberrant-will-taint-be-baked-in","id":291929,"title":"Aberrant - Will \"taint\" be baked in?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-25T02:54:12-07:00","id":291929,"title":"Aberrant - Will \"taint\" be baked in?","content":"Title says it all. I have no problem with &quot;taint&quot; as a concept, but it was pretty much baked into the system and required a lot of kludgy house rules if you wanted to just use the game as a generic Superhero ruleset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3952-magnir","name":"Magnir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T03:15:20-07:00","id":291941,"title":"","content":"Without directly answering your question...<br /> <br /> Honestly, there are dozens of excellent generic superhero rulesets out there. Taint is something that made Aberrant unique and distinct. Why not use one of those other systems instead?<br /> <br /> I mean, granted, you might prefer the ST system, but the new edition won't be the ST system either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T11:18:30-07:00","id":292242,"title":"","content":"Honestly, cutting Taint doesn't require much - you cut the rule about botches in power use generating temporary taint, raising Quantum (or high Node) increasing the permanent one, treat the systems about gaining permanent Taint by decreasing the cost of powers bought as just some sort of tally of flaws/mutations and it's mostly over &amp; you set to go. No big deal really, afaik.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T00:25:37-07:00","id":292775,"title":"","content":"Ian - Because I WANT to use the trappings of the ST system. Are you saying that the new rules won't use the basic dot system interface or that the specifics won't be the Storyteller/Storytelling system? I already know that they are creating a new set of rule within that framework. That doesn't bug me. I'm sure that it will be variant on the tried-and-true rules, not D20 or FATE.<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;taint&quot; isn't the only thing that made Aberrant unique and distinct to me. What made it distinct was that I could create certain childhood characters using the system where I couldn't in many others.<br /> <br /> I also think that the question is fairly irrelevant to my post. It really doesn't matter one way or the other WHY I want to use Aberrant over other Supers games. I just do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Baaldam - I do like the response that amounts to the following when I read it. <br /> Headmaster: All right, settle down, settle down. [He puts his papers down.] Now before I begin the lesson will those of you who are playing in the match this afternoon move your clothes down on to the lower peg immediately after lunch before you write your letter home, if you're not getting your hair cut, unless you've got a younger brother who is going out this weekend as the guest of another boy, in which case collect his note before lunch, put it in your letter after you've had your hair cut, and make sure he moves your clothes down onto the lower peg for you. Now...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3952-magnir","name":"Magnir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T04:21:59-07:00","id":292852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/291929-aberrant-will-taint-be-baked-in?p=292775#post292775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ian - Because I WANT to use the trappings of the ST system. Are you saying that the new rules won't use the basic dot system interface or that the specifics won't be the Storyteller/Storytelling system? I already know that they are creating a new set of rule within that framework. That doesn't bug me. I'm sure that it will be variant on the tried-and-true rules, not D20 or FATE.</div> </div> </div> </div>The new system uses d10s and dice pools, but that's a far cry from saying it's still the ST system. It is not. For several reasons. First and foremost is that the ST System is owned by CCP, while the new system is owned by Onyx Path. If anything should happen to our CCP license, we don't want to lose our mechanics too.<br /> <br /> Second is that the ST system was inadequate for our needs, so we started off fresh from first principles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also think that the question is fairly irrelevant to my post. It really doesn't matter one way or the other WHY I want to use Aberrant over other Supers games. I just do. </div> </div> </div>I'm not trying to tell you what to do, I'm just trying to suss out your reasons. You wanted a generic superhero ruleset, so unless you're using the old Aberrant rules, you'll have to learn new system no matter what. I'm not sure why you'd go with something which more than likely will include something you've already said you don't want, when other options exist which definitely don't have that element.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T09:06:01-07:00","id":292992,"title":"","content":"Could Aberrant <i>be</i> Aberrant without taint?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T20:17:35-07:00","id":293366,"title":"","content":"Probably not.<br /> <br /> That being said, I've used ICONS: Assembled Edition to run a setting based on Adventure! with Aberrant sprinkling before. I'm sure I could do similar with Mutants &amp; Masterminds if I could stand d20 systems.<br /> <br /> My point being that there are a number of very good generics out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T21:33:14-07:00","id":293382,"title":"","content":"A game that is the best, bar none IMO, to accurately do superhero games justice is the DC Heroes MEGS system. It can handle any situation you want to throw at it.<br /> However, I think that Taint helps to define Aberrant. It helps to setup the Aberrants going cuckoo for cocoa puffs and then the Aberrant War. Taking the metaplot out, I love Taint for giving the &quot;power corrupts&quot; angle to Aberrant. It twists their mind and their bodies. It also creates a great mechanic (okay, great in concept but not in implementation) to reign in characters from going to the level of JLA or Authority. That is, without them becoming mutated psychopaths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T23:34:02-07:00","id":293523,"title":"","content":"For my money, old school Aberrant is one of the easiest to use superhero games while still enjoying mechanical rigor. I can make a character faster in Aberrant than I can in most comparable systems. I'd hope that would be a consistent feature with the new setting.<br /> <br /> Taint isn't really that hard to excise as a house-rule, and I am of the personal opinion that games work best when they are crafted for a specific purpose, rather than just being a generic framework. So having taint as part of the default setting seems appropriate to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T23:55:45-07:00","id":294562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/291929-aberrant-will-taint-be-baked-in?p=293366#post293366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably not.<br /> <br /> That being said, I've used ICONS: Assembled Edition to run a setting based on Adventure! with Aberrant sprinkling before. I'm sure I could do similar with Mutants &amp; Masterminds if I could stand d20 systems.<br /> <br /> My point being that there are a number of very good generics out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally. I love Icons and M&amp;M.<br /> <br /> Also, the M&amp;M 2e supplement Paragons includes taint rules for M&amp;M. Probably not too hard to adapt to 3e.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T17:52:55-07:00","id":296345,"title":"","content":"Taint was such an interesting concept I looked at porting to champions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T06:57:46-08:00","id":299955,"title":"","content":"Taint doesn't make Aberrant what it is for me. What makes Aberrant what it is for me is that you can't play Batman, i.e. the badass normal who engages in superhuman combat and wins through superior training etc. In Aberrant, an Elite tears through regular humans, because Novas are very powerful and the game takes a somewhat brutally realistic attitude towards having superhuman power.<br /> <br /> And actually when it comes to supers systems that are not very four colour in terms of how superpowers work on non supers you don't really have many options at all. Aberrant, if it runs solidly, will be the only mainstream example that I can think of. It's very tricky to find a supers game where it takes the tack that you can't run Batman, most of the time supers game strive very hard to ensure that you can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T12:40:08-08:00","id":300314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/291929-aberrant-will-taint-be-baked-in?p=299955#post299955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taint doesn't make Aberrant what it is for me. What makes Aberrant what it is for me is that you can't play Batman, i.e. the badass normal who engages in superhuman combat and wins through superior training etc. In Aberrant, an Elite tears through regular humans, because Novas are very powerful and the game takes a somewhat brutally realistic attitude towards having superhuman power.<br /> <br /> And actually when it comes to supers systems that are not very four colour in terms of how superpowers work on non supers you don't really have many options at all. Aberrant, if it runs solidly, will be the only mainstream example that I can think of. It's very tricky to find a supers game where it takes the tack that you can't run Batman, most of the time supers game strive very hard to ensure that you can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually you can do a Batman type character in Aberrant (one of the players in my group did); technically it would be a Nova but functionally it would be the same as Batman done in most of the four-color superhero games. Aberrant only had one source of power which made the difference more distinct between normal and super, either one had quantum or one did not. In a standard superhero comic or game it is not quite that easy and lines can get quite blurred.<br /> <br /> Batman is not as normal as one may think; in the comics he is shown lifting around 1000lbs on more than one occasion. Even worse, one of the DC games had him able to lift something like 600kg. Back in the early to mid 1980\u2019s there was speculation that he was a low level Meta (or what would be called that in modern DC comics anyway) or part Kryptonian or something similar though that did not seem to go anywhere.<br /> <br /> Similarly, Catwoman has had implied meta-like powers on and off (her penthouse to pavement fall and return to life trick in \u201cBatman Returns\u201d is far from unique for her) since way back to explain how she does (and survives) the things she does in the comics and the movies. Her \u201c9-lives\u201d power has been explained as everything from just luck up to a full suite of powers similar to what Huntress had in the \u201cBirds of Prey\u201d tv series.<br /> <br /> Even the new \u201cGotham\u201d series pilot showed her doing things that would take a Meta to do (though whether intentional or just especially bad Hollywood physics gaffs is yet to be revealed); namely she hopped off a roof and landed in the typical three point crouch on the sidewalk, when the camera pulled back the buildings were 2+ story apartment-over-shop buildings. Later in the same scene, after grabbing a quart or half-gallon jug of milk among other things, she is chased down the street and jumps from the sidewalk up to a fire escape with a locked, caged ladder that the unencumbered adult chasing her obviously considered too high up to be able to continue the chase. Also she claims to be able to see fine details in the dark.<br /> <br /> There generally is a big difference between \u2018normal human\u2019 and Batman level heroes in games; they are usually actually low end supers not too far behind supersoldiers mechanically regardless of whether it makes sense from their backgrounds. Anything less would simply be unplayable with others playing mainline supers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T21:16:05-08:00","id":300731,"title":"","content":"If we are talking Gotham, I suggest mostly bad physics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T11:53:26-08:00","id":301389,"title":"","content":"I got a player who hayes batman for being &quot;normal&quot; yet displaying not normal abilities. I explained it as such-genius child prodigy. Has all the money in the world, so doesnt need to waste time at a job and can train almost constantly. Also-waybetech being a military contractor, as well as having a massive RnD dept. He gets the absolite best toys and gear. He also has a special diet and &quot;vitamin&quot; regiment...basically he is on hgh and very pure &quot;safe&quot; roids...proof? A man in absolute perfect health has a heart attack in his early to mid 50's...clearly from using steroids and other ped's. Bats in aberrant is not quite canon, much more fitted to adventure, but just make a genius level mitoid user, give him all the the background points possible, and all the movatech that all the moneys can buy. And he is a borderline psychopath..if you want to give him some taint...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T11:54:25-08:00","id":301390,"title":"","content":"Sorry for typos-im on my phone and have caveman hands","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T14:11:41-08:00","id":303716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BC001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/291929-aberrant-will-taint-be-baked-in?p=300314#post300314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually you can do a Batman type character in Aberrant (one of the players in my group did); technically it would be a Nova but functionally it would be the same as Batman done in most of the four-color superhero games. Aberrant only had one source of power which made the difference more distinct between normal and super, either one had quantum or one did not. In a standard superhero comic or game it is not quite that easy and lines can get quite blurred.<br /> <br /> Batman is not as normal as one may think; in the comics he is shown lifting around 1000lbs on more than one occasion. Even worse, one of the DC games had him able to lift something like 600kg. Back in the early to mid 1980\u2019s there was speculation that he was a low level Meta (or what would be called that in modern DC comics anyway) or part Kryptonian or something similar though that did not seem to go anywhere.<br /> <br /> Similarly, Catwoman has had implied meta-like powers on and off (her penthouse to pavement fall and return to life trick in \u201cBatman Returns\u201d is far from unique for her) since way back to explain how she does (and survives) the things she does in the comics and the movies. Her \u201c9-lives\u201d power has been explained as everything from just luck up to a full suite of powers similar to what Huntress had in the \u201cBirds of Prey\u201d tv series.<br /> <br /> Even the new \u201cGotham\u201d series pilot showed her doing things that would take a Meta to do (though whether intentional or just especially bad Hollywood physics gaffs is yet to be revealed); namely she hopped off a roof and landed in the typical three point crouch on the sidewalk, when the camera pulled back the buildings were 2+ story apartment-over-shop buildings. Later in the same scene, after grabbing a quart or half-gallon jug of milk among other things, she is chased down the street and jumps from the sidewalk up to a fire escape with a locked, caged ladder that the unencumbered adult chasing her obviously considered too high up to be able to continue the chase. Also she claims to be able to see fine details in the dark.<br /> <br /> There generally is a big difference between \u2018normal human\u2019 and Batman level heroes in games; they are usually actually low end supers not too far behind supersoldiers mechanically regardless of whether it makes sense from their backgrounds. Anything less would simply be unplayable with others playing mainline supers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am well aware of what Batman can do, in a universe where being Batman is within the capabilities of a regular person. What I am saying is that I like that in order to play Batman in Aberrant, you have to either 1) have superpowers or 2) be prepared to die the first time you try and fight a Nova, because Aberrant takes a considerably less flexible attitude towards the capabilities of mortals compared to quantum powered demigods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T00:47:21-08:00","id":304261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/291929-aberrant-will-taint-be-baked-in?p=303716#post303716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am well aware of what Batman can do, in a universe where being Batman is within the capabilities of a regular person. What I am saying is that I like that in order to play Batman in Aberrant, you have to either 1) have superpowers or 2) be prepared to die the first time you try and fight a Nova, because Aberrant takes a considerably less flexible attitude towards the capabilities of mortals compared to quantum powered demigods.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is my point, when you strip away what they say and look instead at what the character actually does then Batman and most of the others of his level really are low level supers. \u201cBeing Batman\u201d is actually NOT within the capabilities of a normal person even in the comics. I have the old DC Heroes game with Batman, Catwoman, and a lot of others on official factory printed cards with their stats and they are definitely not those of a normal person.<br /> <br /> I have already pointed out Batman's unusual strength; his agility and reaction speed are likewise over the top, and he does all this while carrying at least 50 pounds or more of gear. On top of that he does gun kata tricks like aim dodging while taking on a dozen gun armed thugs hand to hand. And that does not even take into account the intelligence and perception tasks that training would take time away from physical training. Speaking of training, it is true that he \u201ctrained up\u201d physically and mentally, but the degree he did that to would be impossible for a single normal person.<br /> <br /> Catwoman is even more outrageous when it comes to impossible physical stunts since she is smaller and has no sign of extra muscle yet keeps up with Batman well enough (and usually surpasses him in agility). She is often seen hanging from the fingers of one hand while working on something with the other, or worse yet hanging upsidedown from a vent or air or skylight shaft without a rope and simply pressing her feet against the walls like River from the Firefly TV series.<br /> <br /> Then there is her 9-lives power. It is often glossed over as \u201cjust luck\u201d letting her get out of jams, but there are too many incidents like the skyscraper fall for that to wash, including getting shot in the temple with a sniper rifle by an assassin Joker sent after her (which he seems to do fairly often). The plastic temple piece of her mask shattered and there was a rather large blood spray which together fooled the assassin into thinking he killed her but when Batman found her she had nothing but a headache and some minor scalp wounds despite the spray on the ground and her clothes (that and it took care of her amnesia that she had for several years prior to the incident though it was later revealed that she was lying about the alternate personality as a way to switch sides and team up with Batman against Joker).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","user":"BC001","date":". 11-06-2014, 03:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T12:46:16-08:00","id":304916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/291929-aberrant-will-taint-be-baked-in?p=293382#post293382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A game that is the best, bar none IMO, to accurately do superhero games justice is the DC Heroes MEGS system. It can handle any situation you want to throw at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me second this assessment. If you want a generic supers setting and you want the gamut from regular schmoe to Superman (or beyond) MEGS can handle it. Check out <a href=\"http://www.writeups.org/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.writeups.org/</a> for a library of comics, film, tv, etc. characters that have been converted on the (very active) mailing list.<br /> <br /> In MEGS is the concept of genre which is where you can adjust the lethality of the game from Captain Carrot to Watchmen.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T05:50:01-08:00","id":310097,"title":"","content":"Um...Batman is actually really easy to make in Aberrant.<br /> <br /> Just spend all your Nova Points on maxing out your Abilities and Attributes, getting a ton of specialties, and maxing out several backgrounds. Throw in a bit of Mega-Int or Perception for detective knacks, and you're set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T10:51:22-08:00","id":310393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spaaace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/291929-aberrant-will-taint-be-baked-in?p=304916#post304916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In MEGS is the concept of genre which is where you can adjust the lethality of the game from Captain Carrot to Watchmen.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>*golf clap* Anyone who knows who Captain Carrot and the Amazing Zoo Crew is deserves a golf clap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T12:07:19-08:00","id":312472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/291929-aberrant-will-taint-be-baked-in?p=310393#post310393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *golf clap* Anyone who knows who Captain Carrot and the Amazing Zoo Crew is deserves a golf clap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I have many fond memories of the Captain and his Crew from when I was a kid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}